course: dictionary
lesson: 2678
title: Diarrhoea: an illness, and how to care for it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diarrhoea is an illness where a person needs the toilet very often, and their poo is runny and watery. «After being sick or having diarrhoea, stay home and sip water.» The sentence tells you what to do when you are ill: rest at home and drink small sips of water.
explain: Germs are often the cause. A tummy bug, called gastroenteritis, is an infection of the stomach and gut, often by norovirus. «Being sick and having diarrhoea is your body throwing the germs out.» That is why washing your hands after the toilet and before eating helps stop it spreading.
explain: When you have diarrhoea, your body loses water quickly, which is called dehydration. «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water so the gut absorbs it well.» Fizzy drinks and fruit juice can make diarrhoea worse, so plain water is the best drink to choose.
fact: Diarrhoea is a noun, and people say have diarrhoea or a bout of diarrhoea.
fact: Dehydration means the body has lost too much water.
fact: The American spelling is diarrhea, without the o.
fact: «Montezuma's revenge» is a joking American name for diarrhoea caught while travelling, especially in Mexico.
fact: The NHS says stay off school until 48 hours after the last time you were sick or had diarrhoea.
exercise: «After being sick or having diarrhoea, stay home and sip water.» What does diarrhoea mean? | Feeling sleepy after lunch | A sweet fizzy drink | A type of sore throat | *An illness where the poo is runny and watery and you need the toilet very often
exercise: Why should you wash your hands after the toilet and before eating? | To make your hands grow bigger | It is only a school rule with no reason | *To help stop the germs that cause diarrhoea spreading | To make the toilet smell nice
exercise: Why must you drink plenty of water when you have diarrhoea? | Water makes you sleepy | Water is only for hot days | Fizzy drinks are better for you | *Your body loses water quickly
test: «Oral rehydration sachets mix salts and sugar in water.» What do the sachets help with? | Getting a sunburn | *Keeping the body's water levels up | Making hair shiny
test: Which drink can make diarrhoea worse? | Plain water | *Fizzy drinks | A small sip of water
exam: The NHS says children should stay off school until when? | Until you have finished your homework | Until the next day | Until the holidays end | *48 hours after the last time you were sick or had diarrhoea
